Subject: [PATCH] TJS2: bounded execution checkpoints for the Android host

Check the VM opcode loop and lexer token entry through a host-owned budget.
The host throws eTJSSilent on cancellation/deadline, which TJS propagates
through script try/catch while preserving upstream frame cleanup. No snapshot
bytes are changed; CMake applies this patch only to the generated copy.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure; Krkr runtime instrumentation timeout/cancel recovery

--- a/src/core/tjs2/tjsInterCodeExec.cpp
+++ b/src/core/tjs2/tjsInterCodeExec.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@

 namespace TJS
 {
+extern void TJSCheckExecutionBudget();
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 // utility functions
 //---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -1009,6 +1010,7 @@
 #endif	// ENABLE_DEBUGGER
 		while(true)
 		{
+			TJSCheckExecutionBudget();
 #ifdef ENABLE_DEBUGGER
 			if( is_enable_debugger ) {
 				tjs_int next_line_no = Block->SrcPosToLine( CodePosToSrcPos(code-CodeArea) );
--- a/src/core/tjs2/tjsLex.cpp
